ABSTRACT 

In the real-time systems project, we study 

#  Real-time software: Models of computation with time and
concurrency, metaprogramming techniques, code generation and
optimization, domain-specific languages, schedulability analysis,
programming of sensor networks.

<p>CGC, DT, schedulability, stochastic models, DE and TM as replacements for Simulink, Giotto, xGiotto, SR.  Aspect-oriented multi-view modeling (quantity managers).  Metropolis as a back end.

